B.yY=new A.d9("sleep","MR. SLEEPWELL","cut","CLASS II \u2014 RESIDENT MASCOT",0,"The picture whitens to a hospital brightness. The station's old bedtime puppet leans into frame, grinning, and a music box starts somewhere behind the wall.","KBLK-7's mascot from the 1968 children's block. The puppet was destroyed on air. It has been coming back to work ever since, always at the end of the shift, always to say goodnight.","CUT the feed. He is a performer \u2014 with no audience and no light he has no reason to stay.","Never answer him with BARS or PATTERN. He takes it as applause.")
B.z0=new A.d9("vert","THE VERTICAL MAN","vhold","CLASS II \u2014 SYNC PARASITE",0,"The picture rolls. In the tear band between frames, for a fraction of a second, something far too tall is standing in the studio.","He exists only in the seam between one frame and the next, which is why nobody has ever photographed him. He is getting taller. The 1981 log has him at four frames. He is now nine.","Lock the sync with V-HOLD. Close the seam and there is nowhere left for him to be.","Do not DEGAUSS a rolling picture. It widens the tear.")
B.z1=new A.d9("dead","DEAD AIR","tone","CLASS III \u2014 ABSENCE",1,"Everything stops. No picture, no grain, no hum \u2014 a silence so total your ears invent things to fill it. One flat green line crosses the screen.","Not an intruder. An appetite. Dead Air is what is left when the signal is removed, and it will keep removing until there is nothing on the frequency at all, including you.","Put something in the silence. The 1000 Hz emergency TONE is the loudest simple thing the desk can make.","Every silent option (CUT, TAPE) makes the hole bigger.")
B.yZ=new A.d9("card","THE TEST CARD GIRL","bars","CLASS III \u2014 REVENANT",1,"Colour bars bleed in from the edges, wrong and oversaturated. A child sits centre frame with a chalk-drawn face and a clown that is not a clown.","She was on the sign-off card from 1971 to 1984. When the card was retired she had nowhere to be, and she has been trying to get back into it ever since. She is not hostile. She is homesick.","Show her the way home. Broadcast BARS and she will step back into the card on her own.","CUT strands her in the dark and she will scream about it.")
B.yW=new A.d9("rerun","THE RERUN","tape","CLASS IV \u2014 LOOP",1,"The image smears into ghost trails. A figure crosses the studio, snaps back, crosses again. The audio echoes a half-second behind itself.","A four-second loop of tape that was never erased, playing since 1976. Whatever was recorded in those four seconds is still happening. It will overwrite anything you transmit with itself.","Give the machine something else to play. Roll fresh TAPE and the loop is broken by new footage.","Anything live \u2014 TONE, BARS, PATTERN \u2014 just gets absorbed into the loop.")
B.yX=new A.d9("niel","THE NIELSEN","pattern","CLASS IV \u2014 AUDITOR",2,"Columns of numbers scroll where the picture should be. A man in a grey suit stands with a clipboard. His head is a bar chart, and it is falling.","He audits. He arrives when the numbers are good and leaves with a portion of them. He does not acknowledge staff, threats, or the fire axe kept in Studio B.","He requires a valid station ident to close the audit. Broadcast the sign-off PATTERN and he files and departs.","He restates the segment output, not the bank. The quota bar walks backward while he files.")
B.z_=new A.d9("call","THE CALLER","hook","CLASS V \u2014 CONTACT",2,"The studio line rings \u2014 every line, at once. An oscilloscope trace fills the screen and speaks. The figure behind it holds a receiver to a head that is only a rotary dial.","It has been trying to reach this station for fifty-one years. It is not calling for you. It is calling for whoever had the shift before you, and it will keep dialling until somebody picks up.","Take it OFF-HOOK and leave the line open. It only needs to be answered, not spoken to.","Do not CUT the call. It redials angrier, and faster.")
